  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "S.Jeyaraj vs / on 8 November, 2024 Author: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan Bench: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan W.P.(MD)No.497 BEFORE THE MADURAI BENCH OF MADRAS HIGH COURT DATED: 08.11.2024 CORAM: THE HONOURABLE MR.JUSTICE G.K.ILANTHIRAIYAN W.P.(MD)No.4977 of 2018 and W.M.P.(MD)No.4967 of 2018 S.Jeyaraj ... Petitio /Vs./ 1.The Adjudicating Officer, The District Revenue Officer, Virudhunagar District. 2.The Designated Officer, Food Safety and Drug, Administration Department (Food Wing), Room.No.203/2015, 2nd Floor, Collectorate Building, Virudhunagar-626 002. 3.The Food Safety Officer, Rajapalayam Municipality, Virudhunagar District. ... Respond PRAYER: Petition filed under Article 226 of the Constitution of Ind issue a Writ of Certiorari to call for the records pertaining to th impugned order of the 1st respondent dated 20.01.2018 passed in cas 11 of 2017-2018 and to quash the same. 1/6 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis W.P.(M For Petitioner : Mr.K.Sudalaiyandi For Respondents : Mr.D.Gandhiraj (R1) S.Jeyaraj vs / on 8 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/190965881/ 1 Special Government Pleader Ms.M.Aasha (R2 & R3) Government Advocate ORDER The sample was sent for a n a l y s i s a n d i t w a s f o u n d t h a t t h e g r o u n d n u t s w e e t w a s m i s b r a n d e d .",
    "facts": "While being so, on 21.02.2017, the third respondent inspected his shop and had taken samples of groundnut sweet. Therefore, the third respondent filed a complaint before the first respondent for the offence punishable under Section 3(1)(zf) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 and Rule 2.2.2(7)(8)(9)(10) of the Food Safety and Standards Rules, 2011, (hereinafter referred to as 'the said Act and Rules' for brevity) as against the petitioner and another.",
    "arguments": "He did not even follow the procedures contemplated under the said Act, while taking sample of the product."
  },
